WEBVTT

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:06.230
We seek the power of the gods, so we can 
use it to return to our human bodies!

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:11.650
Pierce through!

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.080
Why?

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.840
I don't know if you're 
telling the truth or not.

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:23.450
But you said you wanted to be friends.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:24.790
So...

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:31.540
As of this moment, all Wielders
 are to abort the mission.

00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:34.050
This message comes from 
the Japanese government.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.510
We'll let you have this one, Symphogears!

00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:42.630
Let's get out of here, Vanessa!

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.480
Vanessa-san?

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:36.460
<b>Episode 5
The Hidden Thing in the Bag</b>

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.600
Is this for real?

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.120
Our HQ was taken over?

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.360
"Taken over" is a rude way to put it.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.460
Don't you know how to speak the language?

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:46.420
The Disaster Deployment Law for the 
Protection of the Nation, Article 6.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:51.070
If it wishes, the Japanese government is 
given priority authority in all matters

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:54.260
involving special disasters on Japanese soil.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.270
Right?

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:58.150
Correct.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.610
As representatives of
 the Japanese government,

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.070
we are conducting an
 inspection of S.O.N.G.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:07.150
We don't want you treating this 
like some kind of forceful invasion.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:10.210
The public would be very 
upset, so we really don't.

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.330
Sure seems the same to me...

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.460
Don't piss off guys like that.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:18.950
The reason a UN special forces unit is
 allowed to use force on Japanese soil

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:24.550
is because the Japanese government is
 informed beforehand and approves it.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:25.960
Am I wrong?

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.580
You are not!

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:31.230
That's why we submitted the
 official paperwork last year.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:37.600
That weapon I just saw you use wasn't 
in the paperwork we were given.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:38.800
So?

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.780
No... They're using the 
Amalgam as an excuse?

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:45.950
From his tone he was planning on coming up 
with something like that from the start.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:52.040
Commander Kazanari, I believe we should 
accept the government's request.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.130
Indeed.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:59.500
Kiri-chan, they're talking about 
complicated things now, so...

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:05.140
If you don't have anything to hide, 
then you'll allow our inspection, yes?

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:07.410
Very well.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.630
But we have conditions.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:13.360
The Wielders will be allowed to roam freely 
and carry their Gear Converters with them.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:17.470
We're at war, and we need to be 
prepared for the unexpected.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:20.490
That seems fair...

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:26.460
However, you won't be using that new 
unknown weapon until it's approved!

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.910
Whatever!

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:31.920
All right, let's get to work.

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:38.210
That's not some unknown weapon...

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:41.700
It's the courage to unclench your fist...

00:04:42.690 --> 00:04:45.120
They'll never think to look for us here.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.940
I never thought they'd give us this place.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:51.710
Ever since the passing of the DDLPN law,

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:57.270
cleanup of special disasters in Japan
 has fallen under our jurisdiction.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:02.930
Which means that this place is a sanctuary 
for you, one that isn't easily reached.

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:07.290
It's perfect for a hideout.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:11.860
It's time for you to begin 
the last phase of the plan.

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:16.170
You're going to forge the power of the gods 
into a sword the protectors can use.

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:21.370
Everything you need to 
do that is here for you.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:28.800
We've already explained that we're working to 
get the energy you need to use the facilities.

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:32.140
But I have some unfortunate news.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:38.940
There are some people who 
can't do their jobs,

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:43.730
and thanks to them, 
dogs are sniffing around me.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:44.980
That's...

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:52.620
<i>Noble Red was always looked 
down on, treated like objects.</i>

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:57.330
<i>I was a researcher for the 
Faust Robes in the Bavarian Illuminati.</i>

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:00.320
<i>I was critically wounded after an accident.</i>

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:09.790
<i>The lost parts of my body were replaced 
with the Faust Robes that I studied.</i>

00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:12.080
<i>I survived, but...</i>

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:16.930
<i>In an organization which prized 
perfection above all else,</i>

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.940
<i>not only did this lower my standing,</i>

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:26.250
<i>I was further humiliated by being forced 
to undergo clinical trials to gather data.</i>

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:29.510
<i>A hell of pain and humiliation.</i>

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:32.070
<i>The only reason I was able to survive it</i>

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:37.620
<i>was because of Millaarc and Elza, 
my fellow test subjects.</i>

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:43.740
<i>Eventually, our hell came to an end.</i>

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.770
<i>The collapse of the Illuminati 
led to our freedom.</i>

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:54.060
<i>But we had a problem: we couldn't 
survive without special blood.</i>

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:58.520
<i>That's when we met Kazanari Fudou.</i>

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.730
<i>He didn't have a private army,</i>

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:05.060
<i>and in exchange for supplying us with 
blood and helping us achieve our goal,</i>

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:08.130
<i>he wanted us to participate in his plan.</i>

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:15.110
If you are monsters, then you must do your 
job as only monsters can, Noble Red.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:21.340
The plan has begun.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:26.610
And nobody will be allowed to stop it.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:38.440
I figured I'd hear from you.

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:40.000
Are you sure this line is safe?

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:44.750
An informant I was close to during my 
time in the Goyoukiba gave me this line.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:48.310
I've been extremely careful, of course.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:56.210
You were right. The right paperwork 
was filed for this "inspection,"

00:07:56.210 --> 00:08:00.980
but some of the people on the team 
have backgrounds we can't trace.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.240
I see.

00:08:02.240 --> 00:08:05.420
And... There are traces 
of Kamakura's involvement,

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:14.110
Our negotiations with 
the US were at a critical point,

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:16.720
so we let them catch us off-guard, but...

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:22.340
Boss, do you think the one 
giving orders to Noble Red is...

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:23.790
<i>Don't jump to conclusions, Gen.</i>

00:08:24.300 --> 00:08:27.260
Doubt nothing until everything becomes clear.

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:30.400
I want to believe, too.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:34.870
Kazanari Fudou, whatever issues we may have 
with him, is a protector of this country.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:37.640
And he is our father.

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:40.390
<i>Yes, but...</i>

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:42.360
I believe in people.

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:45.960
I'm prepared to believe in them until the end.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.700
And that's why I'm willing 
to do whatever it takes.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:50.970
Brother Yatsuhiro.

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:55.380
<b><u>US-Japan Joint Lunar Discovery
Project Artemis-2</u></b>

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:55.060
That's why I make politics my battlefield.

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:58.840
Relations with the US are bad right now,

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:01.590
but I'm going to make it so we 
can work together with them.

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:08.250
The joint investigation of the lunar ruins 
is just the first step for that.

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:13.610
If things continue to sour, I'm going 
to threaten them with isolation

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:16.940
from international society for 
launching the reactor weapons at us.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:21.390
That'll work well. 
You're amazing, Brother Yatsuhiro.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:24.240
You're the scariest of my brothers.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:27.180
Gen, I'm entrusting the front line to you.

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:31.750
Plans only start to fall apart once 
they've been put into action.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:35.290
If we can grab the tail they 
keep flashing in front of us,

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:37.780
the truth will become clear.

00:09:37.780 --> 00:09:40.310
There'll be plenty of time to doubt then.

00:09:40.710 --> 00:09:41.900
Indeed.

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:46.400
Thanks, ma'am.

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:48.670
Come back anytime.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:58.230
You finally got some time off, 
but you seem down.

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:02.290
Too much has happened...

00:10:03.180 --> 00:10:07.240
Most of the staff are on 
"special alert standby"?

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:09.660
It's all in how you phrase it!

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:13.240
It basically means 
"don't interfere with our inspection."

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:15.500
I like that even less.

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:19.290
But if it's an official request,

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:23.520
the law says that we don't get to refuse.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:25.100
There's nothing we can do.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:26.800
Tsubasa...

00:10:27.550 --> 00:10:31.270
It's not a bad idea to get some rest, but...

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:36.610
<b>Winter Travel</b>

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:36.610
Nobody here is taking things so easy 
that they're going to get excited!

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:40.070
Stare...

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:41.310
No!

00:10:41.310 --> 00:10:43.920
This magazine was just lying around.

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:45.920
It's got nothing to do with anything.

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:50.150
Elfnein-chan, what do you 
do on your days off?

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:52.980
Work off stress.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.920
I use an applied version of 
the direct feedback system

00:10:55.920 --> 00:11:00.020
and by treating the memories in my 
brain region as electrical signals...

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:03.030
Stop it! Stop! Stop it! Stop!

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:07.110
That's not working off stress, 
it's some kind of serious work, probably!

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:08.060
What?

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:11.830
Then that makes me some kind of 
failed alchemist or something

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:14.740
who doesn't know what to do on her days off.

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:18.240
That makes you nothing of the sort!

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:23.690
If that's the problem, spend a few days with 
the perfect way to get rid of your boredom.

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:27.510
Stare.

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:30.090
I'm the perfect way?

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:33.540
Too slow!

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:35.460
Too slow! Too slow!

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.840
What are you doing? No fair.

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.250
Imitating Chris.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:40.250
Is that right?

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:42.430
Is that how Chris-chan acts?

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:44.910
Too slow! Too slow!

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:52.920
So, what will you be doing on your vacation?

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:55.680
I'm not sure... Hmm...

00:11:55.680 --> 00:11:59.650
You haven't had a break in forever. 
What do you want to do?

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:02.660
What do I want to do, huh?

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:29.090
<i>Until the day we meet again, 
the day we can see each other again</i>

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:39.970
<i>I don't want to say why we're saying goodbye</i>

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:34.390
Hibiki, what's going on?

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:36.210
This is strange...

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:40.400
Tsubasa-san's been down lately 
so I wanted to cheer her up...

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:44.220
<i>For some reason I'm just lonely</i>

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:41.850
I'm sorry.

00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:46.530
I took Tachibana up on her offer 
because I suddenly had time, but...

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:49.400
<i>For some reason I just feel empty</i>

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:49.620
I must be pretty stressed.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:51.830
My heart keeps telling me 
I shouldn't be enjoying songs,

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:54.430
<i>Because we both hurt each other</i>

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:55.540
but practicing my skills as a protector.

00:12:54.430 --> 00:12:59.970
<i>and lose everything</i>

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:57.290
I'm getting scared.

00:12:57.730 --> 00:12:59.080
Tsubasa-san.

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:05.120
<i>Together we close the door</i>

00:13:04.670 --> 00:13:07.910
Ever since that day, I haven't 
been able to stop shaking...

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:09.950
<i>Together we erase our names</i>

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:11.360
At my powerlessness, when I 
couldn't save the weak...

00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:20.690
<i>When that times comes our 
hearts will say something</i>

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:14.360
It's all my fault, I tell myself..

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:22.530
This is fun!

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.910
This is another way to spend your days off.

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:27.660
This is kind of fun!

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.300
Hibiki, you're too selfish!

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.740
You don't need to put it that way.

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:32.970
Wait a second.

00:13:32.970 --> 00:13:34.170
Why are you two—

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:38.410
You could've talked to me about Tsubasa-san!

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:40.830
And there were other things 
you could've done!

00:13:40.830 --> 00:13:43.550
I tried my best to come up with an idea...

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:47.270
Your "best" isn't what's important. 
Did you think about Tsubasa-san?

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:50.470
Do you know how Tsubasa-san feels, then?

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:56.470
I do.

00:13:56.470 --> 00:14:00.310
I've always regretted how 
the person I care about

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:03.810
has been in danger, ever since I 
invited them to that concert.

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:10.250
I've never forgiven myself because I'm the 
one who continually puts them in danger.

00:14:11.240 --> 00:14:14.270
I've always hid the words "I'm sorry."

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:18.810
Because I knew it would 
cause trouble for them.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:21.790
Miku... Why?

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:27.110
This is Hibiki. Tsubasa-san 
and Elfnein-chan are with me.

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:30.780
Because S.O.N.G is under inspection,

00:14:30.780 --> 00:14:32.300
I, the inspector's representative,

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.590
<i>will be giving orders.</i>

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:35.770
Who are you?

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:39.230
<i>Alca-Noise signals were 
detected in sector 32.</i>

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:43.820
<i>SG01 and SG03 Dash, the closest to the area,</i>

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:48.020
<i>are to head there and eliminate the targets.</i>

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:54.240
Is that...

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:57.700
You two get somewhere safe!

00:14:57.700 --> 00:15:00.590
Right. Let's go, Elfnein-chan.

00:15:00.590 --> 00:15:01.580
Miku!

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:07.660
We'll talk later.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:11.460
Yeah... You be careful, Hibiki.

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:17.020
Let's go, Tachibana.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:20.340
My clouded blade shall shine 
brightly upon the battlefield!

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:21.450
Right!

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:32.780
<i>Imyuteus Ame no Habakiri tron.</i>

00:16:14.980 --> 00:16:17.840
<i>Countless nights, as the flowers of time fall</i>

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:20.480
<i>I ask myself the question</i>

00:16:20.480 --> 00:16:27.020
<i>Water flows downhill, and people are the same</i>

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:35.780
<i>Cruelly fading from this life (Helplessly)</i>

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:34.090
<b>Thousand Falling Tears</b>

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:40.630
<i>The pinnacle of helplessness (tears drying)</i>

00:16:40.630 --> 00:16:45.910
<i>No, but even cries of sorrow 
can be a blade of judgment</i>

00:16:44.010 --> 00:16:45.930
Fly!

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:51.370
<i>Putting my wishes into this blade 
even though my body may fall apart</i>

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:53.150
<i>SG01 and SG03 Dash, this is a warning.</i>

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:57.810
<i>I will protect, no matter the cost</i>

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.470
<i>Permission for use of unknown 
weapons has not yet been given.</i>

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:56.820
<i>Do not use them.</i>

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:58.090
We know!

00:16:57.810 --> 00:17:07.150
<i>But how much blood must I shed to 
save the flame of life from evil?</i>

00:16:58.090 --> 00:17:02.200
We can handle Alca-Noise without 
Saint Germain and the others' help...

00:17:02.540 --> 00:17:03.720
Don't tell me...

00:17:03.720 --> 00:17:07.030
<i>HQ! Search the area!</i>

00:17:07.030 --> 00:17:10.550
<i>It doesn't make sense that the 
Alca-Noise are out here on their own!</i>

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:10.090
<i>Is there an answer?</i>

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:13.040
<i>Will the light shine?</i>

00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:10.970
<i>They must be...</i>

00:17:10.970 --> 00:17:15.820
Nothing but Alca-Noise signals have
 been detected near the Wielders.

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:17.780
<i>May my sword open a path</i>

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:22.080
<i>SG03 Dash, follow our orders 
and defeat the Alca-Noise.</i>

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:21.450
<i>My sword...</i>

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:27.070
Tachibana, do what HQ tells you 
until the evacuation is complete!

00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:27.860
But...

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:28.720
I'm going!

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:30.990
<i>SG03 Dash.</i>

00:17:30.990 --> 00:17:33.330
<i>If you continue to defy orders,</i>

00:17:33.330 --> 00:17:36.480
<i>you will be stripped of the right 
to take action and arrested...</i>

00:17:36.480 --> 00:17:38.080
The inspection is off.

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.860
The warrant is here!

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:44.650
There's no sign of the inspector!

00:17:45.390 --> 00:17:46.780
He's fast!

00:17:46.780 --> 00:17:48.940
We'll take over control of the battle.

00:17:48.940 --> 00:17:51.760
Ame no Habakiri is heading straight 
into the middle of the enemy!

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:56.420
A sword has a duty!

00:17:56.420 --> 00:17:59.960
A strong power that exists 
to protect the weak!

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:02.470
I'll never let that tragedy happen again!

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.310
There you are...

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:15.740
Damn you!

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:23.970
What?

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:41.850
Tsubasa-san!

00:18:43.880 --> 00:18:44.820
Tsubasa-san!

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:12.630
<i>But how much blood must I shed to 
save the flame of life from evil?</i>

00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:18.380
<i>The heavens shall show me 
the answer and guide me</i>

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:23.250
<i>May my sword open a path</i>

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:26.230
<i>My sword...</i>

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:46.120
<b>Chaos Flame Wrath Slash</b>

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:33.120
Tsubasa... What happened?

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.080
Why?

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:39.740
Why aren't they picking up?

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:43.430
Hibiki

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:43.430
<b>Answer</b>

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:43.430
<b>Decline</b>

00:20:50.810 --> 00:20:53.050
They made this harder than it should be.

00:20:59.140 --> 00:21:01.780
Elfnein-chan! Are you okay?

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:07.200
Elfnein's the clumsy one, right?

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:10.780
Still, you kept me running 
for a good long while.

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:13.970
I won't let you touch my friend!

00:21:13.970 --> 00:21:15.980
No, Miku-san!

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:22.220
I didn't think I could get you 
outside of HQ this easily.

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:24.780
What are you doing here?

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:28.820
I was only ordered to apprehend Elfnein.

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:33.510
Now, I can't decide what 
to do with you on my own.

00:21:35.570 --> 00:21:36.790
Vanessa?

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:39.100
<i>I have a message for you, Millaarc-chan.</i>

00:21:39.100 --> 00:21:41.100
Run, Elfnein-chan!

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:42.640
No, Miku-san.

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:45.920
Yeah, roger.

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:48.990
Don't blame me for this.

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:50.280
Elfnein-chan!

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:52.510
Miku-san, run!

00:21:55.200 --> 00:21:58.620
You never get to see scenes 
like this on TV anymore!

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:01.380
And my body can't control itself!

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:02.830
Miku-san, run!
